SYNTHESIS
  1. The DP-local residual is exactly the old one-far discrepancy, but
     now it appears at every prefix rather than only in a final far step.
  2. The coarse component budget holds on all audited prefixes.  Its slack
     is large in many early/high-support steps, suggesting room for a
     lossy cap-level constant.
  3. The high-pressure steps are finite structured prefixes.  Those are the
     candidates to classify by AP/dyadic/cube-root/Ruzsa address before
     sending the rest to Weyl/BV decorrelation.
